msgstr "Ang characterization suite ay bumubuo ng ilang eksperimento, nagsusumite ng maraming job, at nagfi-fit ng mga resulta, na maaaring umabot sa ilang minuto sa kabuuan. I-enable ang INFO-level logging upang i-print ng bawat stage ang progreso nito habang nangyayari ito.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial does not include a simulator example. The workflow measures the physical imperfections of a specific device: how quickly its qubits relax and dephase, and how often its gates and readout fail. An ideal simulator has none of these imperfections, so there is nothing to characterize. You could attach a synthetic noise model to a fake backend, but the experiments would then only recover the numbers you put in yourself. For that reason, we proceed directly to hardware, broken into the four steps of a Qiskit pattern.\n"
msgstr "Hindi kasama sa tutorial na ito ang isang simulator example. Sinusukat ng workflow ang mga physical imperfection ng isang tiyak na device: kung gaano kabilis nag-relax at nag-dephase ang mga qubit nito, at kung gaano kadalas nabibigo ang mga gate at readout nito. Walang alinman sa mga imperfection na ito ang isang ideal na simulator, kaya walang dapat i-characterize. Maaari kang maglagay ng synthetic noise model sa isang fake backend, ngunit sa gayon ang mga eksperimento ay makukuha lamang ang mga numerong inilagay mo mismo. Dahil dito, direkta tayong magpapatuloy sa hardware, na hinati sa apat na hakbang ng isang Qiskit pattern.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this workflow the \"problem\" is the device itself: the classical inputs are the QPU you want to characterize and the list of properties to measure, and the quantum experiments are the characterization circuits generated from them.\n"
msgstr "Sa workflow na ito, ang \"problema\" ay ang device mismo: ang classical input ay ang QPU na nais mong i-characterize at ang listahan ng mga property na susukatin, at ang quantum na mga eksperimento ay ang mga characterization circuit na nabuo mula sa mga ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, select a backend. This tutorial uses `ibm_kingston`, a 156-qubit Heron r2 processor; you can substitute any IBM Quantum device you have access to (or pick one with `service.least_busy()`).\n"
msgstr "Una, pumili ng backend. Ginagamit ng tutorial na ito ang `ibm_kingston`, isang 156-qubit na Heron r2 processor; maaari kang pumalit ng anumang IBM Quantum device na mayroon kang access (o pumili ng isa gamit ang `service.least_busy()`).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, choose which properties to measure. You can pass any subset of the following experiments:\n"
msgstr "Susunod, piliin kung aling mga properties ang susukatin. Maaari kang magpasa ng anumang subset ng mga sumusunod na eksperimento:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`readout`: SPAM (state preparation and measurement) experiment\n"
msgstr "`readout`: SPAM (state preparation and measurement) na eksperimento\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`rb_1q`: isolated single-qubit randomized benchmarking\n"
msgstr "`rb_1q`: nakahiwalay na single-qubit randomized benchmarking\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`rb_2q`: simultaneous two-qubit randomized benchmarking from a layer fidelity experiment\n"
msgstr "`rb_2q`: sabayang two-qubit randomized benchmarking mula sa layer fidelity na eksperimento\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`t2`: $T_2$ Hahn echo experiment (a single echo by default)\n"
msgstr "`t2`: $T_2$ Hahn echo na eksperimento (iisang echo bilang default)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`t1`: $T_1$ relaxation experiment\n"
msgstr "`t1`: $T_1$ relaxation na eksperimento\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the full suite to get a complete picture of the device; drop entries from the list if you only care about some properties and want to save QPU time.\n"
msgstr "Patakbuhin ang buong suite para makakuha ng kompletong larawan ng device; alisin ang mga entry sa listahan kung mga ilang properties lang ang mahalaga sa iyo at gusto mong makatipid ng oras ng QPU.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Step 2: I-optimize ang problema para sa pagsasagawa gamit ang quantum hardware {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In most tutorials this is where you would transpile your circuits. Here, `BackendCharacterization` takes care of that internally. It builds the experiment circuits directly in the device's native gates, runs the single-qubit experiments on all qubits in parallel, and schedules the two-qubit benchmarking over disjoint layers of the coupling map so that the entire device is covered with a handful of jobs. Because of this parallelization, the whole suite consumes only about 70 seconds of QPU time.\n"
msgstr "Sa karamihan ng mga tutorial, dito mo dapat i-transpile ang iyong mga circuit. Dito, ang `BackendCharacterization` ang bahalang gawin iyon sa loob. Binubuo nito ang mga experiment circuit nang direkta sa native gates ng device, pinapatakbo ang single-qubit experiments sa lahat ng qubit nang sabay-sabay, at itinatakda ang two-qubit benchmarking sa magkakahiwalay na layer ng coupling map para masakop ang buong device gamit lang ang ilang jobs. Dahil sa parallelization na ito, ang buong suite ay umuubos lang ng humigit-kumulang 70 segundo ng oras ng QPU.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Initialize the class that manages the workflow:\n"
msgstr "I-initialize ang class na namamahala sa workflow:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Step 3: Isagawa gamit ang Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `run_experiments` method builds the circuits and submits them as [Sampler](/guides/get-started-with-sampler) jobs. Run it inside a [`Batch`](/guides/run-jobs-batch) context so that the jobs are scheduled together on the QPU, and the method returns once all jobs have been submitted. (You can also run it outside a batch, or inside a `Session`.)\n"
msgstr "Ang `run_experiments` method ang bumubuo ng mga circuit at isinusumite ang mga ito bilang mga [Sampler](/guides/get-started-with-sampler) jobs. Patakbuhin ito sa loob ng [`Batch`](/guides/run-jobs-batch) context para maka-schedule ang mga job nang magkakasama sa QPU, at nagbabalik ang method kapag naisumite na ang lahat ng jobs. (Maaari mo rin itong patakbuhin sa labas ng batch, o sa loob ng `Session`.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"You might see a warning about a backend being passed while a session context manager is open. This is expected and can be safely ignored.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The method returns the submitted jobs as a dictionary keyed by experiment, which is useful for tracking them on the [IBM Quantum Platform dashboard](/guides/monitor-job) or for debugging.\n"
msgstr "Ibinabalik ng method ang mga naisumiteng jobs bilang dictionary na naka-key ayon sa eksperimento, na kapaki-pakinabang para sa pagsubaybay sa mga ito sa [IBM Quantum Platform dashboard](/guides/monitor-job) o para sa debugging.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Step 4: I-post-process at ibalik ang resulta sa nais na classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Analyze the results {#analyze-the-results}"
msgstr "Suriin ang mga resulta {#analyze-the-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `analyze_results` method waits for the jobs to finish and fits the measurement data: exponential decays for $T_1$ and $T_2$, survival-probability decays for the RB experiments, and assignment matrices for readout. It returns a dictionary of *error maps*, one entry per measured property, each mapping a qubit (or qubit pair) to its measured value.\n"
msgstr "Ang `analyze_results` method ay naghihintay para matapos ang mga job at ini-fit ang measurement data: exponential decay para sa $T_1$ at $T_2$, survival-probability decay para sa mga RB experiment, at assignment matrices para sa readout. Nagbabalik ito ng dictionary ng *error maps*, isang entry bawat sinukat na property, bawat isa ay nagmamapa ng qubit (o pares ng qubit) sa sinukat na halaga nito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The maps cover readout error, the single-qubit `x` and `sx` gate errors, the layered two-qubit errors (`lf_error_map`, from the layer fidelity experiment), and the $T_1$ and $T_2$ times in seconds.\n"
msgstr "Sinasaklaw ng mga map ang readout error, ang single-qubit `x` at `sx` gate errors, ang layered two-qubit errors (`lf_error_map`, mula sa layer fidelity na eksperimento), at ang mga oras ng $T_1$ at $T_2$ sa segundo.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Update the backend properties {#update-the-backend-properties}"
msgstr "I-update ang mga backend property {#update-the-backend-properties}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `update_backend` method writes the measured values into the properties of a copy of the backend and returns it. The original `backend` object keeps the reported calibration data, so that we can compare the two, as shown below. Remember that this update is purely local to your Python session; it does not change anything on the device or for other users.\n"
msgstr "Isinusulat ng `update_backend` method ang mga sinukat na halaga sa mga property ng kopya ng backend at ibinabalik ito. Pinapanatili ng orihinal na `backend` object ang naiulat na calibration data, para maikumpara natin ang dalawa, gaya ng ipinapakita sa ibaba. Tandaan na ang update na ito ay lokal lang sa iyong Python session; hindi ito nagbabago ng anuman sa device o para sa ibang users.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare the measured properties against the reported ones {#compare-the-measured-properties-against-the-reported-ones}"
msgstr "Ikumpara ang mga sinukat na property sa mga naiulat na property {#compare-the-measured-properties-against-the-reported-ones}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, plot the measured real-time properties against the values the backend reports. In each panel the qubits (or qubit pairs) are sorted by the measured value, so the measured curve is smooth by construction and the scatter of the reported values around it shows where the two disagree. A single plot is shown for single-qubit RB because the same measured error per gate is assigned to both the `x` and `sx` gates. Axis limits are chosen from the bulk of the data so that a few extreme outliers do not compress the plots; any points outside the range are counted in an annotation on the plot (or pass `ylim` to override the limits).\n"
msgstr "Sa wakas, i-plot ang mga sinukat na real-time property laban sa mga halagang iniulat ng backend. Sa bawat panel, ang mga qubit (o pares ng qubit) ay pinagsunod-sunod ayon sa sinukat na halaga, kaya smooth ang measured curve dahil sa construction nito at ang scatter ng mga naiulat na halaga sa paligid nito ay nagpapakita kung saan hindi magkatugma ang dalawa. Isang plot lang ang ipinapakita para sa single-qubit RB dahil ang parehong sinukat na error kada gate ay itinatalaga sa parehong `x` at `sx` gates. Ang axis limits ay pinipili mula sa bulk ng data para hindi ma-compress ang mga plot ng ilang extreme outlier; ang anumang punto sa labas ng range ay binibilang sa isang annotation sa plot (o ipasa ang `ylim` para i-override ang mga limit).\n"

