msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking/extracted-outputs/cell-25-4.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These plots require a careful reading, because not every gap between the two curves means the device has drifted:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga plot na ito ay nangangailangan ng maingat na pagbabasa, dahil hindi lahat ng puwang sa pagitan ng dalawang curve ay nangangahulugan na nag-drift ang device:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Readout and single-qubit errors**: The measured values track the reported ones for most qubits, while the reported value for a handful of qubits is far off the measured curve. Those localized disagreements are the drift this workflow is designed to catch.\n"
msgstr "**Readout at single-qubit errors**: Sinusundan ng mga sinukat na halaga ang mga naiulat sa karamihan ng mga qubit, habang ang naiulat na halaga para sa ilang qubit ay lubhang malayo sa measured curve. Ang mga naka-localize na hindi pagtutugmang iyon ang drift na dinisenyo ng workflow na ito para mahuli.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**$T_1$**: The two data sets scatter around each other with no systematic offset, which is consistent with $T_1$ fluctuating naturally over time.\n"
msgstr "**$T_1$**: Ang dalawang set ng data ay nag-scatter sa paligid ng isa't isa nang walang systematic offset, na naaayon sa likas na pagbabago-bago ng $T_1$ sa paglipas ng panahon.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Two-qubit errors**: The measured values sit systematically *above* the reported ones. This is expected because the reported values are measured on isolated gates, while the layer fidelity experiment runs many gates simultaneously and therefore includes crosstalk. The layered numbers are more relevant for deep circuits, but they are not directly comparable to the reported calibration data.\n"
msgstr "**Two-qubit errors**: Ang mga sinukat na halaga ay patuloy na *nasa itaas* ng mga naiulat. Ito ay inaasahan dahil ang mga naiulat na halaga ay sinusukat sa nakahiwalay na gates, habang ang layer fidelity na eksperimento ay pinapatakbo ang maraming gates nang sabay-sabay kaya kasama na ang crosstalk. Mas relevant ang layered na mga numero para sa malalalim na circuit, ngunit hindi ito direktang maikukumpara sa naiulat na calibration data.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**$T_2$**: The measured values sit well *below* the reported ones for most qubits. Again, methodology plays a large role, as examined in the next section.\n"
msgstr "**$T_2$**: Ang mga sinukat na halaga ay malinaw na *nasa ibaba* ng mga naiulat para sa karamihan ng qubit. Muli, malaki ang papel ng methodology, na susuriin sa susunod na seksyon.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inspect individual experiment results {#inspect-individual-experiment-results}"
msgstr "Suriin ang mga indibidwal na resulta ng eksperimento {#inspect-individual-experiment-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can also inspect the raw results of the individual characterization experiments through the `experiment_data` property, which returns the underlying [Qiskit Experiments](https://qiskit-community.github.io/qiskit-experiments/) `ExperimentData` objects. For example, the following displays the measured $T_1$ decay curve of a single qubit, which is useful for checking the quality of a fit before trusting the number it produced.\n"
msgstr "Maaari mo ring suriin ang raw na resulta ng mga indibidwal na characterization experiment sa pamamagitan ng `experiment_data` property, na nagbabalik ng mga underlying [Qiskit Experiments](https://qiskit-community.github.io/qiskit-experiments/) `ExperimentData` objects. Halimbawa, ipinapakita ng sumusunod ang sinukat na $T_1$ decay curve ng isang qubit, na kapaki-pakinabang para tiyakin ang kalidad ng fit bago paniwalaan ang numerong nabuo nito.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking/extracted-outputs/cell-28-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking/extracted-outputs/cell-28-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measure T2 with a dynamical decoupling train {#measure-t2-with-a-dynamical-decoupling-train}"
msgstr "Sukatin ang T2 gamit ang dynamical decoupling train {#measure-t2-with-a-dynamical-decoupling-train}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By default the $T_2$ experiment applies a single Hahn echo and measures all qubits in parallel, which, as the comparison plot above showed, can yield noticeably lower $T_2$ values than the backend reports. One hypothesis is the number of echoes: the reported values may be calibrated with dynamical decoupling, which suppresses low-frequency noise. To test this, run a $T_2$-only characterization with `t2_num_echoes` set to a larger value, which applies a CPMG-style train of echo pulses. The delays represent the total free-evolution time in both cases, so the fitted $T_2$ values are directly comparable to the single-echo results.\n"
msgstr "Bilang default, ang $T_2$ na eksperimento ay naglalapat ng iisang Hahn echo at sinusukat ang lahat ng qubit nang sabay-sabay, na, gaya ng ipinakita ng comparison plot sa itaas, ay maaaring magbunga ng mas mababang $T_2$ na halaga kaysa sa iniulat ng backend. Isang hypothesis ay ang bilang ng echoes: maaaring naka-calibrate ang mga naiulat na halaga gamit ang dynamical decoupling, na pumipigil sa low-frequency noise. Para masubukan ito, magpatakbo ng $T_2$-only na characterization na may `t2_num_echoes` na naka-set sa mas malaking halaga, na naglalapat ng CPMG-style na train ng echo pulses. Kumakatawan ang mga delay sa kabuuang free-evolution time sa parehong kaso, kaya direktang maikukumpara ang mga fitted na halaga ng $T_2$ sa mga resulta ng single-echo.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking/extracted-outputs/cell-31-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking/extracted-outputs/cell-31-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this run the extra echoes barely changed the result: the 8-echo median (56 &micro;s) is close to the single-echo one (53 &micro;s), and both remain far below the reported median (142 &micro;s). The number of echoes alone does not explain this gap; other methodological differences are involved, such as calibration procedure details, measuring all qubits in parallel rather than in isolation, and so forth.\n"
msgstr "Sa run na ito, halos hindi nagbago ang resulta dahil sa dagdag na echoes: ang 8-echo median (56 &micro;s) ay malapit sa single-echo (53 &micro;s), at pareho pa ring lubhang mas mababa sa naiulat na median (142 &micro;s). Ang bilang lang ng echoes ay hindi sapat para ipaliwanag ang gap na ito; may iba pang methodological na pagkakaiba na kasangkot, tulad ng mga detalye ng calibration procedure, pagsukat sa lahat ng qubit nang sabay-sabay sa halip na nakahiwalay, at iba pa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The practical lesson is to treat $T_2$ (and layered two-qubit error) comparisons across methodologies with care. The refreshed values are a self-consistent snapshot taken under conditions close to a real workload, which makes them well suited for comparing qubits against each other or tracking a device over time. A gap relative to the reported calibration data, however, is not automatically evidence of drift.\n"
msgstr "Ang praktikal na aral ay ang pag-ingat sa paghahambing ng $T_2$ (at layered two-qubit error) sa iba't ibang methodology. Ang mga na-refresh na halaga ay isang self-consistent na snapshot na kinuha sa ilalim ng mga kondisyong malapit sa aktwal na workload, na ginagawa itong angkop para sa paghahambing ng mga qubit sa isa't isa o pagsubaybay sa device sa paglipas ng panahon. Ang isang gap kaugnay ng naiulat na calibration data, gayunpaman, ay hindi awtomatikong ebidensya ng drift.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Steps 1–4 compressed into a single call {#steps-14-compressed-into-a-single-call}"
msgstr "Steps 1–4 na pinagsama-sama sa iisang tawag {#steps-14-compressed-into-a-single-call}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For day-to-day use you rarely need the intermediate results. The `run_and_update` method chains everything you did above (building, submitting, fitting, and updating) into a single call that returns the refreshed backend. It accepts the same `experiments` list (and forwards options such as `t2_num_echoes`), and can likewise be wrapped in a `Batch` or `Session` context.\n"
msgstr "Para sa pang-araw-araw na paggamit, bihira mong kailanganin ang mga intermediate na resulta. Ang `run_and_update` method ay pinagtatagni-tagni ang lahat ng ginawa mo sa itaas (paggawa, pagsusumite, pag-fit, at pag-update) sa iisang tawag na nagbabalik ng na-refresh na backend. Tinatanggap nito ang parehong `experiments` list (at ipinapasa ang mga opsyon tulad ng `t2_num_echoes`), at maaari rin itong i-wrap sa `Batch` o `Session` context.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"The following cell does not return until all jobs and post-processing are done.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The refreshed `backend_updated` object is now ready to be used wherever backend properties feed into your workflow. Try out this process in conjunction with the [Real-time benchmarking for qubit selection](/tutorials/real-time-benchmarking-for-qubit-selection) tutorial to choose the best-performing qubits when transpiling a circuit. Because the device keeps drifting, refresh the properties close to the time you actually execute your workload.\n"
msgstr "Handa na ngayong gamitin ang na-refresh na `backend_updated` object saanman kinakailangan ng backend properties sa iyong workflow. Subukan ang proseso na ito kasabay ng [Real-time benchmarking for qubit selection](/tutorials/real-time-benchmarking-for-qubit-selection) na tutorial para piliin ang mga qubit na may pinakamahusay na performance kapag nag-transpile ng circuit. Dahil patuloy na nag-drift ang device, i-refresh ang mga property malapit sa oras na aktwal mong isasagawa ang iyong workload.\n"

